WEBVTT

1
00:00:02,402 --> 00:00:06,440
♪♪

2
00:00:12,179 --> 00:00:15,148
[ Static crackling ]

3
00:00:21,789 --> 00:00:30,632
♪♪

4
00:00:30,732 --> 00:00:39,406
♪♪

5
00:00:39,507 --> 00:00:48,950
♪♪

6
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:57,625
♪♪

7
00:00:57,725 --> 00:01:04,832
♪♪

8
00:01:04,933 --> 00:01:11,438
♪♪

9
00:01:11,539 --> 00:01:12,740
-Grandpa?

10
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:15,810
♪♪

11
00:01:15,910 --> 00:01:17,444
Is that you?

12
00:01:17,545 --> 00:01:20,180
♪♪

13
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:23,851
It's me.
You don't recognize my voice?

14
00:01:23,952 --> 00:01:28,455
♪♪

15
00:01:28,556 --> 00:01:31,291
Listen -- I can only talk
for a few minutes.

16
00:01:31,391 --> 00:01:34,862
♪♪

17
00:01:34,963 --> 00:01:36,496
I'm in trouble.

18
00:01:37,832 --> 00:01:39,801
I'm in serious trouble.

19
00:01:43,037 --> 00:01:44,505
Can you help me?

20
00:01:47,274 --> 00:01:49,711
I was in an accident...

21
00:01:51,278 --> 00:01:53,313
...a really bad accident.

22
00:01:55,617 --> 00:02:00,187
They say...They're saying
I might have to go to jail.

23
00:02:03,691 --> 00:02:07,528
I know that sounds bad, Grandpa,
but it's not my fault.

24
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:14,401
You can't tell anyone
about this, okay?

25
00:02:17,572 --> 00:02:19,874
You're the only person
I can trust.

26
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:24,812
I have to tell you
one more thing,

27
00:02:24,912 --> 00:02:26,748
and please don't be mad.

28
00:02:30,618 --> 00:02:32,419
They want money.

29
00:02:33,721 --> 00:02:36,724
They want money,
or they're not letting me go.

30
00:02:36,958 --> 00:02:40,061
-[ Chuckles ] That's right.

31
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,829
When do they need it?

32
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:45,499
-They need it right now,
Grandpa.

33
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:49,704
♪♪

34
00:02:49,804 --> 00:02:52,740
This is serious.
Don't you want to help me?

35
00:02:53,975 --> 00:02:56,811
You're not just going to leave
me here, are you?

36
00:02:58,746 --> 00:03:00,648
-That's great.

37
00:03:00,748 --> 00:03:02,482
-Please, Grandpa.

38
00:03:03,316 --> 00:03:04,952
-You're scared.

39
00:03:06,154 --> 00:03:08,089
-I'm so, so scared.

40
00:03:08,188 --> 00:03:09,489
-[ Chuckles ]

41
00:03:10,825 --> 00:03:12,994
-Will you help me?

42
00:03:13,094 --> 00:03:15,830
-"I need you to help me."

43
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:17,932
-I need you to help me.

44
00:03:18,966 --> 00:03:20,467
Help me!

45
00:03:21,135 --> 00:03:22,704
Oh, God, help me!

46
00:03:23,336 --> 00:03:25,707
Please, Grandpa.

47
00:03:25,807 --> 00:03:28,543
Please, Grandpa.

48
00:03:28,643 --> 00:03:30,243
-"I need you!"

49
00:03:31,012 --> 00:03:32,747
-Help me!

50
00:03:32,847 --> 00:03:36,684
-Say it. "I need you."

51
00:03:36,784 --> 00:03:38,218
-I need you.

52
00:03:38,318 --> 00:03:40,220
-[ Pitifully] "I need you."

53
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:41,856
-I need you.

54
00:03:41,956 --> 00:03:43,791
-[ Chuckles ]

55
00:03:43,891 --> 00:03:45,660
-Help me!
-[ Chuckles ]

56
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,061
-Help me!

57
00:03:47,161 --> 00:03:48,495
-That's great.

58
00:03:48,596 --> 00:03:53,701
-Help me, help me, help me!

59
00:03:54,969 --> 00:03:56,336
Help me.

60
00:04:02,777 --> 00:04:05,646
[ Water dripping ]

61
00:04:06,547 --> 00:04:09,349
[ Indistinct chatter ]

62
00:04:17,992 --> 00:04:19,392
-Ms. Sadik...

63
00:04:19,493 --> 00:04:22,930
So, you're guaranteed
to find them...

64
00:04:23,030 --> 00:04:25,967
[ Indistinct chatter ]

65
00:04:28,002 --> 00:04:29,003
-So, where? Where is it?

66
00:04:29,103 --> 00:04:31,239
-In Aurora.
-In Aurora.

67
00:04:31,338 --> 00:04:34,274
[ Indistinct chatter continues ]

68
00:04:35,042 --> 00:04:38,646
-Uh, but she's just been...

69
00:04:43,017 --> 00:04:44,018
-Yes.

70
00:04:48,156 --> 00:04:50,323
[ Woman laughs ]

71
00:04:50,423 --> 00:04:52,660
[ Indistinct chatter continues ]

72
00:04:56,898 --> 00:05:00,001
-But nothing -- you know,
I wouldn't freak out just yet.

73
00:05:00,101 --> 00:05:09,944
♪♪

74
00:05:10,044 --> 00:05:13,147
[ Indistinct chatter continues ]

75
00:05:13,247 --> 00:05:18,152
♪♪

76
00:05:18,252 --> 00:05:25,458
♪♪

77
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:29,496
-Ms. Sadik, I appreciate you
coming on such short notice.

78
00:05:29,597 --> 00:05:30,798
-Oh, it's no problem.

79
00:05:30,898 --> 00:05:31,933
-Have a seat.

80
00:05:32,033 --> 00:05:35,303
I have a mountain of paperwork
for you to sign.

81
00:05:35,402 --> 00:05:36,637
[ Sighs ]

82
00:05:36,737 --> 00:05:38,973
We've had a fair amount
of turnover lately.

83
00:05:39,073 --> 00:05:41,108
It's been a challenge
finding the right match

84
00:05:41,209 --> 00:05:42,877
for this patient.

85
00:05:42,977 --> 00:05:44,245
He's difficult.

86
00:05:44,344 --> 00:05:46,981
Um, eccentric on a good day.

87
00:05:47,081 --> 00:05:48,549
-What's his condition?

88
00:05:48,649 --> 00:05:49,884
-The family moved him in here

89
00:05:49,984 --> 00:05:52,320
when he started hitting
on the housekeeper.

90
00:05:52,419 --> 00:05:54,655
He thought she was his wife.

91
00:05:54,755 --> 00:05:57,525
They thought possibly
early-onset Alzheimer's.

92
00:05:57,625 --> 00:05:59,894
We're still ruling things out.

93
00:05:59,994 --> 00:06:02,330
Listen -- I know you
don't have a lot of experience,

94
00:06:02,429 --> 00:06:05,266
but I have a good feeling
about you.

95
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:07,668
-I'd really like
to be helpful here.

96
00:06:08,502 --> 00:06:10,137
-The pool is closing
for the day.

97
00:06:10,238 --> 00:06:12,039
Please return to your villas.

98
00:06:12,139 --> 00:06:20,882
♪♪

99
00:06:20,982 --> 00:06:29,090
♪♪

100
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:38,366
♪♪

101
00:06:38,465 --> 00:06:47,742
♪♪

102
00:06:47,842 --> 00:06:50,177
[ Door opens ]

103
00:06:50,278 --> 00:06:54,115
♪♪

104
00:06:54,215 --> 00:06:57,084
♪♪

105
00:06:57,985 --> 00:06:59,320
[ Door closes ]

106
00:06:59,419 --> 00:07:01,756
[ Indistinct chatter ]

107
00:07:03,824 --> 00:07:06,027
-I think that's the wrong size.

108
00:07:07,295 --> 00:07:09,630
-Oh, I kind of like it baggy.

109
00:07:15,569 --> 00:07:17,204
-Here. Why don't you try this?

110
00:07:18,606 --> 00:07:21,943
Are you working days or nights?

111
00:07:22,043 --> 00:07:23,978
-I'm on nights.

112
00:07:24,078 --> 00:07:27,648
-Nights are really special.
You'll see.

113
00:07:29,884 --> 00:07:35,790
There you go. See?
That fits perfect.

114
00:07:42,697 --> 00:07:45,465
It's amazing to be needed,
isn't it?

115
00:07:46,934 --> 00:07:49,971
It feels good
to mean something to somebody...

116
00:07:51,539 --> 00:07:54,709
...to be absolutely necessary,
you know?

117
00:07:56,043 --> 00:07:57,244
-Thank you.

118
00:07:57,345 --> 00:08:00,715
-Sure.
I'll see you around.

119
00:08:03,217 --> 00:08:07,655
♪♪

120
00:08:07,755 --> 00:08:10,024
[ Indistinct chatter ]

121
00:08:10,124 --> 00:08:11,826
♪♪

122
00:08:11,926 --> 00:08:14,595
[ Quacking ]

123
00:08:16,630 --> 00:08:19,967
[ Birds chirping ]

124
00:08:20,067 --> 00:08:28,342
♪♪

125
00:08:28,442 --> 00:08:36,784
♪♪

126
00:08:36,884 --> 00:08:45,159
♪♪

127
00:08:45,259 --> 00:08:54,101
♪♪

128
00:08:54,201 --> 00:08:58,906
♪♪

129
00:08:59,006 --> 00:09:06,814
♪♪

130
00:09:06,914 --> 00:09:08,215
-Before we begin the test,

131
00:09:08,315 --> 00:09:11,385
I want you to remember
this list of words, okay?

132
00:09:11,485 --> 00:09:16,724
Face, pink, satin, box, tree.

133
00:09:27,234 --> 00:09:29,270
Now I'm going to read you
a list of letters,

134
00:09:29,370 --> 00:09:31,439
and you're going to tap
your head with your hand

135
00:09:31,540 --> 00:09:34,041
each time you hear
the letter "A," okay?

136
00:09:36,143 --> 00:09:37,344
-The letter "A."

137
00:09:37,445 --> 00:09:38,846
-That's right.

138
00:09:40,549 --> 00:09:47,721
"F," "B," "A," "C."

139
00:09:49,423 --> 00:09:51,759
[ Birds chirping ]

140
00:09:52,059 --> 00:09:58,999
"B," "A," "B."

141
00:10:01,570 --> 00:10:03,904
Can you tell me
the day of the month?

142
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:08,142
-I don't know.

143
00:10:08,242 --> 00:10:10,377
-And what about
the day of the week?

144
00:10:11,879 --> 00:10:13,647
-I don't keep track.

145
00:10:14,682 --> 00:10:15,883
-And where are we right now?

146
00:10:15,983 --> 00:10:17,618
Do you know where you are?

147
00:10:17,718 --> 00:10:19,521
-In a house.

148
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:21,155
Not my house. [ Inhales ]

149
00:10:22,056 --> 00:10:23,991
My house didn't look like this.

150
00:10:24,091 --> 00:10:27,161
It looked different.
It was better.

151
00:10:27,261 --> 00:10:29,763
-And what were those words
I told you to remember?

152
00:10:29,864 --> 00:10:32,099
Can you name them?

153
00:10:32,199 --> 00:10:35,669
-The words?
-Yes, the five words.

154
00:10:35,769 --> 00:10:37,304
Do you remember them?

155
00:10:40,575 --> 00:10:42,843
-I was never good at school.

156
00:10:49,216 --> 00:10:51,252
[ Lighter flicks ]

157
00:10:56,357 --> 00:10:57,892
Do you want one of these?

158
00:10:59,693 --> 00:11:01,295
-Don't let him scare you, Eleni.

159
00:11:01,395 --> 00:11:05,366
He's just a bored, old man.

160
00:11:05,466 --> 00:11:14,441
♪♪

161
00:11:14,543 --> 00:11:23,552
♪♪

162
00:11:23,652 --> 00:11:29,524
♪♪

163
00:11:29,624 --> 00:11:31,058
All right.

164
00:11:34,596 --> 00:11:36,764
I'm not an invalid.

165
00:11:36,864 --> 00:11:40,167
-Yes, you are. Don't be stupid.

166
00:11:40,467 --> 00:11:42,836
Can you get us some towels?

167
00:11:47,576 --> 00:11:52,313
-Stop! Stop, stop. Stop.

168
00:11:53,881 --> 00:11:57,985
Stop it.
You're getting water everywhere.

169
00:12:01,021 --> 00:12:02,990
Oh, my God. Look at me.

170
00:12:03,991 --> 00:12:06,260
You learn to play along.

171
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:07,895
It's easier that way.

172
00:12:09,664 --> 00:12:12,099
-Hey, Mona?

173
00:12:12,399 --> 00:12:15,202
[ Chuckles ] Mona?

174
00:12:15,302 --> 00:12:17,371
I need you.

175
00:12:17,471 --> 00:12:24,478
♪♪

176
00:12:24,579 --> 00:12:34,121
♪♪

177
00:12:34,221 --> 00:12:42,731
♪♪

178
00:12:42,830 --> 00:12:49,403
♪♪

179
00:12:52,206 --> 00:12:53,541
-He's all yours.

180
00:13:04,351 --> 00:13:07,121
[ Insects chirping ]

181
00:13:08,989 --> 00:13:11,859
[ Dogs barking in distance ]

182
00:13:38,152 --> 00:13:40,220
-Is that better, Mr. Callum?

183
00:13:49,296 --> 00:13:50,831
-It isn't right.

184
00:13:54,034 --> 00:13:55,537
-Well, tell me how you want it.

185
00:13:55,637 --> 00:13:57,905
-I should be taking care of you.

186
00:14:00,441 --> 00:14:02,142
-But I'm the nurse.

187
00:14:03,977 --> 00:14:05,513
-That doesn't matter.

188
00:14:12,986 --> 00:14:14,922
Let me take care of you.

189
00:14:24,198 --> 00:14:26,367
-[ Whispering ]
Let me take care of you.

190
00:14:28,902 --> 00:14:30,871
Let me take care of you.

191
00:14:32,439 --> 00:14:34,942
Let me take care of you.

192
00:14:35,876 --> 00:14:38,245
Let me take care of you.

193
00:14:38,345 --> 00:14:39,514
♪♪

194
00:14:39,614 --> 00:14:43,050
[ Laughter ]

195
00:14:43,150 --> 00:14:45,854
[ Indistinct chatter ]

196
00:14:45,986 --> 00:14:55,496
♪♪

197
00:14:55,597 --> 00:14:58,232
♪♪

198
00:14:58,332 --> 00:14:59,466
♪♪

199
00:14:59,567 --> 00:15:01,468
-Mmm...

200
00:15:01,569 --> 00:15:04,405
♪♪

201
00:15:04,506 --> 00:15:12,012
♪♪

202
00:15:12,112 --> 00:15:13,380
You want to make sure
that one arm is

203
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,750
firmly around their waist
like this,

204
00:15:15,850 --> 00:15:22,489
so that they feel secure, and
keep their other arm real tight.

205
00:15:23,957 --> 00:15:26,160
-I'm supposed to be sleeping.

206
00:15:27,361 --> 00:15:28,530
-It's okay.

207
00:15:31,566 --> 00:15:37,204
Tell them to put one foot
in front of the other like that.

208
00:15:43,477 --> 00:15:49,450
And you really want to make sure
that they don't go too deep.

209
00:15:49,551 --> 00:15:52,219
[ Laughs ]
You can't let go of them.

210
00:15:52,319 --> 00:15:53,320
Tell me.

211
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:55,489
-Uh, make sure they
don't go too deep.

212
00:15:55,590 --> 00:15:56,591
-Yeah.
-Don't let go.

213
00:15:56,691 --> 00:15:58,660
-Yeah, exactly.

214
00:16:04,031 --> 00:16:06,200
Douglas? Douglas?

215
00:16:07,702 --> 00:16:09,269
You want to come in?

216
00:16:10,672 --> 00:16:12,507
-I like watching you girls.

217
00:16:22,282 --> 00:16:24,485
-Where were you working
before this?

218
00:16:25,687 --> 00:16:27,522
-I...wasn't.

219
00:16:28,121 --> 00:16:30,658
[ Indistinct chatter ]

220
00:16:32,694 --> 00:16:34,596
I took some time off.

221
00:16:36,363 --> 00:16:39,266
-The girls said you
got fired from your last job.

222
00:16:42,002 --> 00:16:44,238
-It was just a misunderstanding.

223
00:16:46,975 --> 00:16:48,408
-Did you...I mean,

224
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:50,945
you seem
to be taking to it very well.

225
00:16:51,044 --> 00:16:54,749
-Oh, um, thank you.
-Yeah.

226
00:16:55,415 --> 00:17:01,656
-I wasn't myself for a while,
but I like it here.

227
00:17:01,756 --> 00:17:09,531
♪♪

228
00:17:09,631 --> 00:17:18,540
♪♪

229
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:20,875
♪♪

230
00:17:20,975 --> 00:17:23,243
[ Dings ]

231
00:17:23,343 --> 00:17:32,854
♪♪

232
00:17:32,954 --> 00:17:42,530
♪♪

233
00:17:42,630 --> 00:17:50,337
♪♪

234
00:17:50,437 --> 00:17:54,509
♪♪

235
00:17:59,413 --> 00:18:00,582
-Water.

236
00:18:19,867 --> 00:18:22,369
[ Water running ]

237
00:18:43,323 --> 00:18:44,491
[ Glass clangs ]

238
00:19:14,187 --> 00:19:15,857
What's your name again?

239
00:19:17,725 --> 00:19:19,027
-Eleni.

240
00:19:19,127 --> 00:19:20,394
-Eleni.

241
00:19:21,896 --> 00:19:25,867
That's nice. I like that.

242
00:19:27,602 --> 00:19:28,936
-Thank you.

243
00:19:29,236 --> 00:19:33,473
-And what do you do, Eleni, hmm?

244
00:19:35,643 --> 00:19:36,711
-I'm a nurse.

245
00:19:36,811 --> 00:19:40,815
-I know you're a nurse.
What do you do for fun?

246
00:19:43,518 --> 00:19:46,754
-I don't know.
I don't do anything.

247
00:19:46,854 --> 00:19:49,489
-You're telling me
you don't have any fun?

248
00:19:56,130 --> 00:19:58,599
-I have fun helping my patients.

249
00:20:00,768 --> 00:20:03,705
-Yeah. I bet you do.

250
00:20:13,781 --> 00:20:15,348
-[ Exhales ]

251
00:20:16,818 --> 00:20:19,687
[ Insects chirping ]

252
00:20:41,274 --> 00:20:43,611
[ Chirping continues ]

253
00:20:50,718 --> 00:20:53,020
Sorry.
I accidentally fell asleep.

254
00:20:53,121 --> 00:20:54,622
-Hey. Good morning.

255
00:20:54,722 --> 00:20:56,891
-You're supposed
to be sleeping.

256
00:20:56,991 --> 00:20:58,726
-I'm gonna make a call.

257
00:20:59,961 --> 00:21:01,696
-In the middle of the night?

258
00:21:02,730 --> 00:21:03,898
-It's business.

259
00:21:05,233 --> 00:21:06,801
-What business?

260
00:21:08,903 --> 00:21:10,805
-Can you repeat after me?

261
00:21:11,539 --> 00:21:12,974
-Who are you calling?

262
00:21:13,074 --> 00:21:15,543
-Just repeat after me. Okay?

263
00:21:15,643 --> 00:21:19,514
"Grandpa, I can only talk
for a few minutes."

264
00:21:19,881 --> 00:21:20,882
-I don't understand.

265
00:21:20,982 --> 00:21:23,684
-Just do it.

266
00:21:27,522 --> 00:21:30,925
-Grandpa, I can only talk
for a few minutes.

267
00:21:31,025 --> 00:21:32,627
-[ Whispering ] Do you hear him?

268
00:21:36,496 --> 00:21:40,067
[ Normal voice ] "I was in
an accident. I hurt someone.

269
00:21:40,168 --> 00:21:43,538
They say I might
have to go to jail."

270
00:21:44,772 --> 00:21:49,277
-I was in an accident.
I hurt someone.

271
00:21:49,710 --> 00:21:51,112
-[ Whispering ] "They say..."

272
00:21:51,212 --> 00:21:54,182
-They say I might
have to go to jail.

273
00:21:54,282 --> 00:21:55,550
-"Wait by the phone.

274
00:21:55,650 --> 00:21:59,419
My lawyer's gonna call
you right now, okay?"

275
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:00,822
-Wait by the phone.

276
00:22:00,922 --> 00:22:03,825
My lawyer is going to call
you right now, okay?

277
00:22:03,925 --> 00:22:05,492
-"I love you."

278
00:22:08,162 --> 00:22:09,664
